# Production installs runtime dependencies only (skip devDependencies).
#
# Why: the hosting platform bundles the full node_modules into its deploy
# archive. With devDependencies installed, vitest pulls in vite -> esbuild,
# and esbuild ships its binary as a HARDLINK
#   node_modules/esbuild/bin/esbuild  ->  node_modules/@esbuild/linux-x64/bin/esbuild
# The platform's tar cannot recreate that hardlink on extract and aborts the
# deploy with:
#   Failed to extract archive: tar: can't create hardlink
#   './node_modules/esbuild/bin/esbuild' to './node_modules/@esbuild/linux-x64/bin/esbuild'
#
# Nothing in production needs the dev tree: next build's toolchain (typescript,
# tailwind, postcss, autoprefixer) lives in "dependencies", and next.config.ts
# sets eslint.ignoreDuringBuilds. Omitting dev removes the esbuild hardlink and
# shrinks the archive.
#
# Local note: to run the test suite (vitest), install with
#   npm install --include=dev
omit=dev
